    "created_at": "2020-04-24T11:29:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-24T11:29:22Z",
    "body": "I believe this has to do with how WSL 2 optimizes FS access between the virtual Linux disk and the Windows physical disk:\r\n\r\n> You will notice slower file speeds compared to WSL 1 when accessing Windows files from a Linux application, or accessing Linux files from a Windows application. This is a result of the architectural changes in WSL 2, and is something that the WSL team is actively investigating on how we can improve this experience\r\n\r\n[[source]](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/wsl2-ux-changes#cross-os-file-speed-will-be-slower-in-initial-preview-builds)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
